{
  "id": "ss.base.finds",
  "name": "The finds store",
  "description": "Where the camp keeps what the ruins handed over between expeditions: a lean-to store beside the arms locker, put up out of the lander's skin and the expedition's racks. A corrugated slab of hull plate for a roof, rusted at one end; a steel frame round an open front, and inside, in the dark against a back of riveted plates, two uprights and three shelves with the finds on them in rows as if catalogued: a carved chip of the ruins' stone, a ring of it, a tablet cut with a zigzag, a jar with a finger of jelly; a shard with the signal still in its seam (the one pink thing), a carved bowl, a flake of carapace, a tied bundle with its tag; on the bottom a crate of the smaller ones and a long slab leaning on the upright. The cage door stands swung open, steel mesh in a frame, a padlock hanging open on it; the inventory is pinned to the left post; the crates the finds came home in are stacked outside. In feelers the pocket is packed at it.",
  "tags": ["base"],
  "size": [90, 80],
